WEBVTT

00:00:00.434 --> 00:00:03.699
Lolly Inclusive Design Policy

00:00:04.683 --> 00:00:08.765
Last updated: 30 July 20 26

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.694
Our ethos.

00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:15.762
An open source community includes all of

00:00:15.824 --> 00:00:16.818
us.

00:00:17.608 --> 00:00:20.118
Software that anyone can read, run and

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:22.932
change only earns that openness when

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.800
anyone can actually use it - whatever they

00:00:25.914 --> 00:00:29.120
see, hear, process, speak or believe.

00:00:29.915 --> 00:00:32.875
So we treat accommodation as a form of

00:00:32.954 --> 00:00:36.480
celebration, never a compromise: a

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:38.581
preference that makes Lolly calmer,

00:00:38.641 --> 00:00:41.536
louder, larger or more familiar for

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:44.281
someone is not a degraded mode of the

00:00:44.342 --> 00:00:45.544
product.

00:00:46.297 --> 00:00:49.315
It is the product, meeting one more of us

00:00:49.376 --> 00:00:50.919
where they are.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.541
What this policy covers

00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:58.907
Lolly is a creative tool: people come here

00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:01.694
to make things that represent them.

00:01:02.454 --> 00:01:05.175
That shapes every accommodation below in

00:01:05.235 --> 00:01:08.474
one specific way - adjusting the app never

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.370
adjusts your work.

00:01:11.148 --> 00:01:13.995
Accessibility preferences restyle Lolly's

00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:17.724
own interface: menus, cards, navigation,

00:01:17.793 --> 00:01:18.819
type.

00:01:19.585 --> 00:01:22.383
They are engineered never to reach inside

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:26.190
the tool canvas or the export pipeline,

00:01:26.258 --> 00:01:29.406
and automated tests fail our builds if a

00:01:29.468 --> 00:01:32.331
preference could move a single pixel of an

00:01:32.407 --> 00:01:34.219
exported file.

00:01:34.992 --> 00:01:37.465
You should never have to choose between a

00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:40.795
comfortable app and a faithful render.

00:01:41.928 --> 00:01:43.699
Accessibility

00:01:44.275 --> 00:01:58.375
Beyond following the platform's own signals «system dark mode, the OS reduced-motion preference», Lolly ships explicit, opt-in accessibility preferences on your profile:

00:01:59.111 --> 00:02:01.952
Reduce motion turns off transitions,

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:05.379
slides and animated flourishes in the

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:12.100
app, and combines with «never overrides» your operating system's setting.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:17.725
Animated exports keep moving exactly as designed.

00:02:18.463 --> 00:02:21.391
High contrast strengthens borders, text

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:24.344
and focus rings around your work.

00:02:25.141 --> 00:02:28.482
Your brand colours and canvas stay exactly

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.318
as you set them.

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:34.145
Large text grows the app's type and icon

00:02:34.207 --> 00:02:36.647
glyphs without reflowing your

00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:40.205
designs, so what you export is

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:41.993
byte-identical.

00:02:42.751 --> 00:02:44.907
Hide colourful previews swaps the

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:48.181
gallery's preview artwork for calm icon

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.771
and text cards, and softens project

00:02:51.847 --> 00:02:54.180
thumbnails, halving their colour and

00:02:54.241 --> 00:02:56.843
contrast, so they stay recognisable

00:02:56.895 --> 00:02:59.020
without the colour noise.

00:02:59.804 --> 00:03:02.393
Full colour returns the moment you step

00:03:02.456 --> 00:03:05.192
inside a tool, so the one place

00:03:05.283 --> 00:03:08.285
high-stimulus imagery appears is the one

00:03:08.347 --> 00:03:11.144
place you chose to work on it.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:14.978
You can set these for yourself right now:

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:17.502
open your Accessibility settings - the

00:03:17.623 --> 00:03:20.760
four switches above, on one plain card, no

00:03:20.822 --> 00:03:21.894
digging.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.706
Alongside the preferences: controls carry

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.010
accessible names and pressed states,

00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:30.287
changes are announced to screen readers,

00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:32.568
overlays close on Escape, the drawing

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:34.758
tools answer single keypresses and the

00:03:34.817 --> 00:03:36.555
arrow keys nudge whatever you have

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:39.629
selected, keyboard focus is visible and

00:03:39.689 --> 00:03:42.176
strengthened further under high contrast

00:03:42.251 --> 00:03:44.439
and every one of these switches is a

00:03:44.527 --> 00:03:47.488
plain, always-visible card on the profile

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:48.644
page -

00:03:49.423 --> 00:03:52.064
findable by someone who can barely read

00:03:52.123 --> 00:03:55.604
the page as it is, which is the moment it

00:03:55.665 --> 00:03:56.894
matters.

00:03:57.693 --> 00:03:58.859
Listen.

00:03:59.649 --> 00:04:02.593
Eleven core pages of this documentation

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.590
can be read aloud - play, pause and follow

00:04:05.651 --> 00:04:08.876
the words as they are spoken, at a pace

00:04:08.936 --> 00:04:10.169
you set.

00:04:10.953 --> 00:04:14.031
Narration is English-only for now, and

00:04:14.092 --> 00:04:16.969
more pages are being recorded.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:21.205
Slowing down costs nothing in quality: it

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.728
is a different speed, not a lesser one,

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.020
for anyone who learns at their own pace.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.453
Reduced and enhanced stimulation

00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:35.557
Neurodivergent people are not one audience

00:04:35.613 --> 00:04:37.219
with one need.

00:04:37.991 --> 00:04:40.797
The same brain that is overwhelmed by a

00:04:40.885 --> 00:04:44.101
wall of colourful thumbnails on a hard day

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:47.364
may seek strong sensory input on another,

00:04:47.456 --> 00:04:50.559
so Lolly accommodates in both directions,

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.419
always opt-in:

00:04:53.197 --> 00:04:55.293
Turning it down.

00:04:56.073 --> 00:04:59.023
Reduce motion and Hide colourful previews

00:04:59.106 --> 00:05:00.234
strip the

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:06.025
interface back to icons, text and one accent colour.

00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:24.975
Navigation stays busy-free for people with ADHD, autistic people and dyslexic people who find dense, high-variance imagery hard to scan; nothing you need «favourites, pinning, actions» is taken away in the calmer presentation.

00:05:25.719 --> 00:05:27.543
Turning it up.

00:05:28.337 --> 00:05:31.286
Neurospicy Mode is a deliberate sensory

00:05:31.347 --> 00:05:32.846
layer - focus

00:05:33.809 --> 00:05:36.081
loops, an atmosphere mixer with

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:38.866
individually levelled ambient beds,

00:05:38.927 --> 00:05:41.354
procedural music and interface sound

00:05:41.387 --> 00:05:44.515
effects - for people who focus best with

00:05:44.599 --> 00:05:46.094
rich input.

00:05:46.857 --> 00:05:50.297
It is off by default and never auto-plays

00:05:50.359 --> 00:05:52.119
before you ask.

00:05:52.926 --> 00:05:55.293
Sound is separable.

00:05:56.056 --> 00:05:59.107
Every audible layer has its own switch, so

00:05:59.152 --> 00:06:00.319
"visuals

00:06:01.228 --> 00:06:04.683
calm, sound rich" and the reverse are both

00:06:04.759 --> 00:06:07.635
real configurations, not a single

00:06:07.704 --> 00:06:10.349
accessibility bundle someone else composed

00:06:10.425 --> 00:06:11.670
for you.

00:06:12.822 --> 00:06:16.598
Language and localization priority

00:06:17.564 --> 00:06:20.594
Lolly's interface and documentation are

00:06:20.656 --> 00:06:23.945
translated into more than 25

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:28.396
languages, and we prioritise languages by

00:06:28.458 --> 00:06:31.715
how many people speak them, not by market

00:06:31.786 --> 00:06:34.714
revenue - Hindi, Bengali, Urdu and

00:06:34.774 --> 00:06:38.031
Indonesian arrived in the same waves as

00:06:38.124 --> 00:06:39.994
French and German.

00:06:40.768 --> 00:06:43.375
Right-to-left scripts are first-class:

00:06:43.451 --> 00:06:46.867
Arabic ships with full RTL layout, not

00:06:47.804 --> 00:06:50.443
a mirrored afterthought.

00:06:51.245 --> 00:06:53.278
Languages are distinct, not

00:06:53.328 --> 00:06:56.607
interchangeable: Indonesian and Malay are

00:06:56.698 --> 00:06:57.609
separate

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.337
catalogs, Traditional and Simplified

00:07:01.398 --> 00:07:04.451
Chinese are separate catalogs and the

00:07:04.511 --> 00:07:07.049
language attribute is set before first

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.462
paint so Han characters and script

00:07:09.525 --> 00:07:12.071
fallbacks render correctly for your

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.969
language, not a lookalike.

00:07:15.739 --> 00:07:18.407
The language menu lists every language in

00:07:18.439 --> 00:07:21.935
its own name and script, and can be

00:07:22.763 --> 00:07:26.043
ordered by speaker population, so finding

00:07:26.105 --> 00:07:28.772
yours never requires knowing its English

00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:29.869
name.

00:07:30.984 --> 00:07:33.096
Cultural inclusion

00:07:34.011 --> 00:07:36.585
The neutral starting brand assumes nothing

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.739
about who you are; Lolly exists so

00:07:40.684 --> 00:07:43.424
your own identity, palette and type

00:07:43.474 --> 00:07:45.919
replace ours in minutes.

00:07:46.686 --> 00:07:49.925
Type is treated as a cultural surface:

00:07:49.994 --> 00:07:52.956
uploaded and Google fonts are shaped

00:07:53.883 --> 00:07:56.919
with proper text shaping across scripts,

00:07:57.008 --> 00:08:00.428
so names, diacritics and non-Latin text

00:08:00.487 --> 00:08:03.482
export as correctly drawn outlines rather

00:08:03.542 --> 00:08:06.344
than tofu or substitutions.

00:08:07.103 --> 00:08:09.752
Copy avoids idioms and culture-bound

00:08:09.813 --> 00:08:12.985
references that translate poorly, and

00:08:13.956 --> 00:08:17.100
translators receive clean, bare strings

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:19.516
rather than sentences with markup

00:08:19.581 --> 00:08:21.469
fragments baked in.

00:08:22.591 --> 00:08:25.272
Why this produces better work, not just

00:08:25.343 --> 00:08:26.852
kinder software

00:08:27.853 --> 00:08:31.032
Accessibility gets filed under compliance,

00:08:31.084 --> 00:08:34.543
which quietly frames it as a cost.

00:08:35.324 --> 00:08:37.468
It is not one.

00:08:38.234 --> 00:08:40.645
The same properties that make a tool

00:08:40.705 --> 00:08:43.844
usable on a hard day make it faster on

00:08:43.933 --> 00:08:47.020
every other day, and they compound.

00:08:47.795 --> 00:08:51.818
Cognitive endurance is the real budget.

00:08:52.611 --> 00:08:55.608
Attention is finite and it

00:08:56.607 --> 00:08:58.993
drains unevenly.

00:08:59.755 --> 00:09:02.715
Every dialog you dismiss, every setting

00:09:02.769 --> 00:09:05.525
that resets, every choice a template

00:09:05.587 --> 00:09:08.098
should have made for you spends a little

00:09:08.158 --> 00:09:11.070
of what you had left for the work.

00:09:11.827 --> 00:09:14.380
Constraint-first tools spend almost none

00:09:14.413 --> 00:09:17.850
of it: the brand decisions were made once,

00:09:17.917 --> 00:09:20.683
at the tool, so producing the twentieth

00:09:20.733 --> 00:09:23.519
asset costs what the first did.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:27.019
People who need that most feel it first,

00:09:27.077 --> 00:09:29.845
and everyone benefits from it.

00:09:30.624 --> 00:09:34.393
Creative confidence comes from safety.

00:09:35.189 --> 00:09:35.856
When

00:09:36.904 --> 00:09:39.419
any output could be wrong in a way you

00:09:39.475 --> 00:09:42.180
will only discover later, you check

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:45.270
everything twice and stay cautious.

00:09:46.044 --> 00:09:49.194
When off-brand output is not reachable,

00:09:49.256 --> 00:09:51.943
the checking stops being your job and the

00:09:52.015 --> 00:09:54.719
caution goes back into the work.

00:09:55.474 --> 00:09:58.980
Confidence is not a mood, it is a property

00:09:59.036 --> 00:10:00.844
of the constraints.

00:10:01.631 --> 00:10:05.143
The value of tools is compounding.

00:10:05.905 --> 00:10:09.367
A decision set by a tool is correct every

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:10.375
time

00:10:11.283 --> 00:10:13.947
that tool runs, in every language, at

00:10:14.022 --> 00:10:17.619
every size, for everyone who uses it.

00:10:18.386 --> 00:10:21.234
A rule written in some style guidelines

00:10:21.298 --> 00:10:24.558
doc is only as influential when it is

00:10:24.622 --> 00:10:25.669
read.

00:10:26.437 --> 00:10:29.525
With no promise of correct output to the

00:10:29.588 --> 00:10:30.643
reader.

00:10:31.414 --> 00:10:34.398
The difference is small at first; huge

00:10:34.459 --> 00:10:37.419
when multiplied by every task.

00:10:38.205 --> 00:10:40.839
What protects the workflow protects the

00:10:40.902 --> 00:10:42.118
person.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.367
On-device rendering,

00:10:46.129 --> 00:10:49.456
plain-file exports and offline capability

00:10:49.567 --> 00:10:52.767
are usually filed under privacy, and they

00:10:52.846 --> 00:10:55.519
are also what keeps you working on a bad

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.612
connection, on a locked-down machine or

00:10:58.671 --> 00:11:01.519
the day a subscription lapses.

00:11:02.303 --> 00:11:05.102
Your workflow does not have dependencies

00:11:05.193 --> 00:11:07.169
you did not choose.

00:11:07.947 --> 00:11:10.219
Two things follow that we treat as

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:13.970
inseparable: operational superiority,

00:11:14.031 --> 00:11:16.075
because software that respects your

00:11:16.131 --> 00:11:19.107
attention and your data is simply faster

00:11:19.198 --> 00:11:22.296
to work in, and ethics that cannot be

00:11:22.358 --> 00:11:24.337
traded away, because they are

00:11:24.425 --> 00:11:27.269
architectural rather than promised.

00:11:28.044 --> 00:11:31.918
A policy can be revised under pressure.

00:11:32.701 --> 00:11:35.862
An engine that never receives your content

00:11:35.929 --> 00:11:38.319
has nothing to revise.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.369
Ethical commitments

00:11:42.278 --> 00:11:45.118
Privacy by architecture.

00:11:45.927 --> 00:11:49.043
Your work stays on your device.

00:11:49.828 --> 00:11:51.306
There are no

00:11:52.285 --> 00:11:55.643
trackers or analytics in the codebase, and

00:11:55.692 --> 00:11:58.801
the few network touchpoints are enumerated

00:11:58.863 --> 00:12:01.019
in the Privacy Policy.

00:12:01.788 --> 00:12:04.689
Accessibility and language preferences are

00:12:04.776 --> 00:12:08.545
stored in your own profile, on your device

00:12:08.633 --> 00:12:11.455
- a person's disability or language is

00:12:11.534 --> 00:12:13.245
never telemetry.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:17.426
Telemetry is no friend of this project: we

00:12:17.461 --> 00:12:20.034
don't want it, and nobody should have to

00:12:20.095 --> 00:12:22.145
give their data away.

00:12:22.928 --> 00:12:24.943
Honest provenance.

00:12:25.704 --> 00:12:29.344
Exports can carry Content Credentials, and

00:12:30.374 --> 00:12:34.743
AI-generated content is labelled as such.

00:12:35.515 --> 00:12:38.406
We believe audiences deserve to know how

00:12:38.466 --> 00:12:42.130
media was made, and creators deserve tools

00:12:42.188 --> 00:12:45.020
that can prove their work is theirs.

00:12:45.834 --> 00:12:48.143
No dark patterns.

00:12:48.894 --> 00:12:51.609
Preferences are plain switches that do

00:12:51.671 --> 00:12:53.194
what they say,

00:12:53.575 --> 00:13:06.275
defaults are dormant until you choose them and platform conventions «native scrolling, browser shortcuts, standard dialogs» are respected rather than hijacked.

00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:08.919
Open source.

00:13:09.696 --> 00:13:13.041
The engine, shells and community tools are

00:13:13.103 --> 00:13:14.219
public.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:15.696
Every

00:13:16.613 --> 00:13:19.183
claim in this document is checkable in the

00:13:19.284 --> 00:13:22.840
source, and several are enforced by tests

00:13:22.899 --> 00:13:25.112
that fail the build when broken - the

00:13:25.208 --> 00:13:28.087
additive-by-default rule for accessibility

00:13:28.147 --> 00:13:30.988
attributes, the ban on preferences

00:13:31.061 --> 00:13:33.665
reaching exports and the keeping-in-step

00:13:33.698 --> 00:13:35.924
of the app's two copies of each

00:13:35.985 --> 00:13:37.269
preference.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.051
Holding ourselves to it

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:51.850
Inclusive design here is a policy in the engineering sense: invariants with tests, not aspirations with adjectives.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:14:08.425
When an accommodation and a feature conflict, we redesign the feature «when a 'hide previews' setting also hid icons off utility cards, the fix was to keep the actions, not to excuse the loss».

00:14:08.775 --> 00:14:19.900
If something in Lolly excludes you - a missing language, an overwhelming moment, an assumption we baked in without noticing - that is a bug.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.700
Tell us: fitzy@suse-com.
